      "id": "n1uzehq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5.1 Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC)"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC) provides a systematic sequence of phases for building high-quality software.",
        "SDLC models vary in methodology, ranging from traditional linear models to modern iterative and agile frameworks.",
        "Software testing strategies are categorized based on structural knowledge: Black Box, White Box, and Grey Box testing.",
        "Software metrics quantify software quality, complexity, maintainability, and process productivity.",
        "Design patterns offer proven, reusable solutions to recurring object-oriented design and architectural problems."
      ],
      "id": "juejh65"
    },
